# Ministral preprocessor routing — DRAFT, NOT APPLIED
#
# Base commit: 9b82320 (the quota governor). Applies cleanly to public/app.js at that commit.
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#   Adds `window._preprocessorRoute` ('small' | '8b' | '14b') to the Scene-1 PROMPT_PREPROCESSOR
#   dispatch, selecting between mistral-small-latest, ministral-8b-2512 and ministral-14b-2512,
#   and omits `reasoning_effort` for the Ministral models (they do not accept the parameter).
#   The json_object contract is unchanged.
#
# WHY IT IS NOT COMMITTED
#   The default is 'small', so applying it changes nothing by itself — but it is the first half
#   of a routing change, and the second half (the proxy allowlist, in the sibling patch) is what
#   makes it reachable. Neither should land before the prerequisites in
#   _audit_out/migration_handoff_2026-09-04.md §7 are met: notably a frozen input corpus for the
#   preprocessor (which means storing prompt content — an open scope decision) and an authorized
#   spend ceiling for the 8B-vs-14B comparison.
#
# MEASURED CONTEXT
#   The preprocessor request is ~85 KB (~21k nominal tokens) and does not fit Mistral Small's
#   20,000 TPM bucket. Both 8B (625k TPM / 3.13 RPS) and 14B (937.5k TPM / 0.5 RPS) solve
#   throughput, so the choice is contract quality, not capacity. 14B has the TIGHTEST rate in the
#   family — one request per 2 s — despite the second-largest TPM.
#
